                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Great Action Game, but a Flawed Remake for Longtime Fans[/h1]\r\n\r\nAs someone who has played every single Resident Evil game from the 1996 original to the modern entries, my feelings on the Resident Evil 3 Remake are highly conflicted. It is a fantastic, polished action-horror game, but a disappointing adaptation of a survival horror classic.\r\n\r\n[b]Pros:[/b]\r\n[list]\r\n[*] [b]Exceptional Combat:[/b] The core gameplay feels incredible. The addition of the perfect dodge mechanic makes Jill Valentine feel incredibly agile, adding a fun, high-skill ceiling to the action.\r\n[*] [b]Stunning Visuals:[/b] The RE Engine continues to shine. Raccoon City looks beautifully chaotic, and the character models, lighting, and gore effects are stellar.\r\n[*] [b]High Replay Value:[/b] While a single run is brief (around 5–6 hours), unlocking the in-game Shop for infinite ammo weapons and modifiers makes tackling the brutal Nightmare and Inferno difficulties highly addictive.\r\n[/list]\r\n\r\n[b]Cons:[/b]\r\n[list]\r\n[*] [b]Massive Content Cuts:[/b] It is impossible to ignore how much Capcom cut from the 1999 original. Losing iconic areas like the Clock Tower and the Park hurts, and removing the branching choices takes away from the narrative replay value.\r\n[*] [b]Nemesis is Too Scripted:[/b] Coming off the terrifying, unpredictable stalker AI of Mr. X in RE2 Remake, Nemesis is a letdown. Most of his appearances are heavily scripted set-pieces and linear boss battles.\r\n[*] [b]Rushed Pacing:[/b] The game pushes you forward at a breakneck speed, leaving very little room for the slow-burn atmospheric exploration and puzzle-solving that defines classic Resident Evil.\r\n[/list]\r\n\r\n[b]Verdict: 8/10.[/b] If you judge it strictly as a standalone action-horror title, it's a blast. But if you are coming into this expecting the same faithful, expansive treatment that RE2 and RE4 received, lower your expectations. Definitely grab it on a Steam sale!\r\n",
